  "expect": {
    "kind": "good",
    "note": "The second of the two CLAUDE.md reference fixtures, and the one the first must not be swapped with. This file carries the ELECTRON BOOKKEEPING half only: three arrows to build the bridge, two to open it, and the bromonium rather than an open carbocation as the intermediate, which is what makes the addition anti. It does NOT carry the stereochemistry, and it cannot: the v1 conservation fixture schema deliberately has no stereo fields, which fixture-schema.ts states and gives its reason for. At this level of description this fixture is byte for byte the same mechanism as good-bromine-addition-to-cis-2-butene-via-a-bromonium-ion apart from the substrate name, which is itself the finding worth recording: nothing in the conservation family can tell the racemic outcome from the meso one, so nothing in the conservation family can catch the sign error CLAUDE.md warns about. That distinction is asserted in bromine-addition-to-2-butene-racemic-against-meso.oracle.json against RDKit CIP labels and RDKit meso detection, where trans-2-butene gives the chiral C2 symmetric bromonium and the single meso product, the exact inverse of the cis case."
